# Line endings that survive a Windows checkout into the container.
#
# A shell script written on Windows gets CRLF if git's autocrlf converts it - and
# /bin/sh in the container then fails with ``no such file or directory`` for a file
# that clearly exists: it is the \r it cannot find. The entrypoint is the file this
# kills, so its endings are pinned.
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
